      "message": ".first() -\u003e .one()\n\n... and then wrap that call into a try/except, catching sql.NotFound.\n\none() has a slightly different behavior in that it raises an exception instead of returning None, and it\u0027ll also raise an exception if more than one result is found, which would appropriately result in a 500. (.first() suppresses that condition by simply returning the first result).",
